    "markdown": "---\ntitle: \"03. Compaction and scatter-add: work proportional to the data\"\ndescription: \"Select the few particles that matter at each step (x[mask], push!) and scatter them into a histogram at data-dependent indices.\"\njupyter: python3\n---\n\n\n\n## The problem\n\n$N$ particles move with fixed velocities on the periodic interval $[0, 1)$. At each of\n$T = 50$ steps, a narrow window sweeps across the domain. The particles inside it,\nabout 1 %, are deposited with linear (cloud-in-cell) weights into a histogram $H$ of\n1024 bins. A taper $w(d) = (1 - |d|/h_w)^2$ fades the contribution to zero at the\nwindow edges, which keeps the loss differentiable as particles enter and leave. We\ndifferentiate\n$$\\mathcal{L}(x_0) = \\lVert H(x_0) - H_{\\text{target}} \\rVert^2$$\nwith respect to the initial positions.\n\nTwo irregular patterns are involved:\n\n- **Compaction.** The work worth doing is proportional to the number of *selected*\n  particles, which changes with the data: `x[mask]`, `findall`, `push!` into a buffer.\n- **Scatter-add** at data-dependent indices: `H[j] += w`.\n\nThe same patterns appear in event detection, active-set methods, particle-in-cell\ndeposits, histogramming, and resampling.\n\n## Code\n\n::: {.panel-tabset group=\"impl\"}\n## Enzyme.jl (CPU)\n{{< embed enzyme.qmd#loss-cpu echo=true >}}\n{{< embed enzyme.qmd#grad-cpu echo=true >}}\n\n## Enzyme.jl (GPU)\n{{< embed enzyme.qmd#loss-gpu echo=true >}}\n{{< embed enzyme.qmd#grad-gpu echo=true >}}\n\n## JAX\n{{< embed jax.qmd#loss echo=true >}}\n{{< embed jax.qmd#grad echo=true >}}\n:::\n\n## Same gradient\n\n::: {#e09018f5 .cell execution_count=2}\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=2}\n```{=html}\n<style type=\"text/css\">\n</style>\n<table id=\"T_5f6b1\">\n  <thead>\n    <tr>\n      <th id=\"T_5f6b1_level0_col0\" class=\"col_heading level0 col0\" >implementation</th>\n      <th id=\"T_5f6b1_level0_col1\" class=\"col_heading level0 col1\" >‖g‖₂</th>\n      <th id=\"T_5f6b1_level0_col2\" class=\"col_heading level0 col2\" >max rel. diff vs enzyme</th>\n    </tr>\n  </thead>\n  <tbody>\n    <tr>\n      <td id=\"T_5f6b1_row0_col0\" class=\"data row0 col0\" >enzyme</td>\n      <td id=\"T_5f6b1_row0_col1\" class=\"data row0 col1\" >52854.055962</td>\n      <td id=\"T_5f6b1_row0_col2\" class=\"data row0 col2\" >0.0e+00</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td id=\"T_5f6b1_row1_col0\" class=\"data row1 col0\" >jax</td>\n      <td id=\"T_5f6b1_row1_col1\" class=\"data row1 col1\" >52854.055962</td>\n      <td id=\"T_5f6b1_row1_col2\" class=\"data row1 col2\" >4.9e-14</td>\n    </tr>\n  </tbody>\n</table>\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\nThe gradients differ at the 1e-14 level, not 1e-16, because scatter-adds into the same\nbin are summed in a different order.\n\n## Timings\n\nFloat64, $T = 50$ steps, median of 3–10 runs after warm-up.\n\n::: {#11300f49 .cell execution_count=3}\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=3}\n```{=html}\n<div style=\"height:100%; width:100%;\">                        <script>window.PlotlyConfig = {MathJaxConfig: 'local'};</script>\n        <script charset=\"utf-8\" src=\"https://cdn.plot.ly/plotly-4.1.1.min.js\" integrity=\"sha256-O24V1F27f8pb0glCkelh3cVHLNiHAJ5gCaVtq2aNch8=\" crossorigin=\"anonymous\"></script>                <div id=\"6736a1a8-69c2-4d3f-be75-afc16ccdcee1\" class=\"plotly-graph-div\" style=\"height:100%; width:100%;\"></div>            <script>                window.PLOTLYENV=window.PLOTLYENV || {};                                if (document.getElementById(\"6736a1a8-69c2-4d3f-be75-afc16ccdcee1\")) {                    Plotly.newPlot(                        \"6736a1a8-69c2-4d3f-be75-afc16ccdcee1\",                        [{\"hovertemplate\":\"implementation=enzyme (cpu)\\u003cbr\\u003eN=%{x}\\u003cbr\\u003egradient time [s]=%{y}\\u003cextra\\u003e\\u003c\\u002fextra\\u003e\",\"legendgroup\":\"enzyme (cpu)\",\"line\":{\"color\":\"#636efa\",\"dash\":\"solid\"},\"marker\":{\"symbo